<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian official reserves rise in March.</title>
<headline>Australian official reserves rise in March.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's holdings of gold and foreign exchange assets rose to US$17.122 billion in March from US$16.822 billion in February, compared with US$13.977 billion in March 1996, the Reserve Bank of Australia said. In Australian dollar terms, reserves rose by A$87 million to A$21.770 billion in March from A$21.683 billion in February and compared with A$17.935 billion a year earlier, the bank said.  </p>
<p>Individual reserve assets in Australian dollars were -</p>
<p>			     Mar 1997	  Feb 1997	 Mar 1996</p>
<p>    Gold		3.50 billion    3.65 billion   4.02 billion</p>
<p>    SDRs		  40 million	45 million     64 million</p>
<p>IMF Reserve position</p>
<p>			   587 million     600 million    631 million</p>
<p>Foreign Exchange</p>
<p>			 17.65 billion   17.39 billion  13.22 billion</p>
<p>    TOTAL:	   21.77 billion   21.68 billion  17.94 billion</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
